Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?phlink:=20phase=205-02=20=E2=80=94=20real=20adb?=
 =?UTF-8?q?lock=20C++=20wrapper=20via=20cxx::bridge?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the 5-02a smoke consumer with a proper Rust↔C++ bridge layer
over the vendored adblock-rust crate (Brave, MPL-2.0).

Layout (mirrors //components/qr_code_generator):

* chrome/browser/phlink/adblock/phlink_adblock_ffi.rs
  - cxx::bridge exposing engine_new_empty / engine_new_from_rules /
    engine_should_block. Returns a plain BlockDecision struct so 5-03
    won't need another FFI roundtrip when it starts honoring
    `important` and `redirect`. Malformed URLs fail open
    (matched=false) per PRD §6.

* chrome/browser/phlink/adblock/phlink_adblock.{h,cc}
  - Thin C++ owner class `phlink::adblock::Engine` with
    CreateEmpty / CreateFromRules / ShouldBlock. Holds a
    rust::Box<EngineHandle>; concrete engine state is opaque to C++.

* chrome/browser/phlink/adblock/phlink_adblock_unittest.cc + test()
  target `phlink_adblock_unittests` — 4 gtest cases (empty engine,
  malformed URL fails open, host block, exception rule).

Also: drop default-features for adblock so the engine is built without
the `single-thread` feature. The Mutex-protected build is Send+Sync,
which simplifies the per-thread plumbing in 5-03 vs. the original D-06
atomic-swap design. Verified during research: URLLoaderRequestInterceptor
is documented as navigation-only, so 5-03 will use
ContentBrowserClient::CreateURLLoaderThrottles instead.

Validation:
  autoninja -C out/Default phlink_adblock_unittests
  ./out/Default/phlink_adblock_unittests
  → SUCCESS: all tests passed (4/4).

Refs PRD §5 (perf, ad blocking), ADBL-01.
